Consider the classes `C` and `CDemo` shown here:

```java
class C<T>
{
    T data;
    C(T t) { data = t; }
}
class CDemo
{
    public static void main(String[] args)
    {
        C<Object> co = new C<String>("Hi");
        C<Integer> ci = new C<33>(44);
        C<int> ci = new C<int>(3);
        C<String> cs = new C<String>("Hi");
        String[ ] s = {"a", "b", "c"};
        C < String [ ] > csa = new C <String [ ] >(s);
    }
}
```

Which of the statements in the `main( )` method of `CDemo` are illegal? Explain what is wrong with the illegal statements.
